# MantleCMS conventions

MantleCMS predates the SelfHosted layout, so the shared solution-structure and DI rules don't apply here.

- Modular: `Mantle.*` libraries with `.Abstractions` splits, plus `Plugins/Mantle.Plugins.*`. The DI container is swappable (`Mantle.Infrastructure.Autofac`/`DryIoc`/`Lamar`/`LightInject`/`DotNetDefault`).
- Register services through Dependo's `IDependencyRegistrar` in `Infrastructure/DependencyRegistrar.cs`, not `ServiceCollectionExtensions`:
```csharp
public class DependencyRegistrar : IDependencyRegistrar
{
    public void Register(IContainerBuilder builder, ITypeFinder typeFinder, IConfiguration configuration)
    {
        if (!PluginManager.IsPluginInstalled(Constants.PluginSystemName))
        {
            return;
        }

        builder.Register<ISettings, RedisCacheSettings>(ServiceLifetime.Scoped);
        builder.RegisterNamed<ICacheManager, RedisCacheManager>("Mantle_Cache_Static", ServiceLifetime.Singleton);
    }

    public int Order => 99999;
}
```
- Plugins check `PluginManager.IsPluginInstalled` before registering. Each plugin has its own `Constants.PluginSystemName`.
- Data access goes through `IGenericDataService<T>` / `GenericDataService<T>` (Mantle.Data) on top of the Extenso repository. Entity maps implement `IMantleEntityTypeConfiguration`, and seeding uses `IDbSeeder`/`ISupportSeed`.
- Some UI and grid code uses `Extenso.AspNetCore.Mvc.ExtensoUI`, Kendo (`Extenso.KendoGridBinder`) and OData.
- Tests use xUnit.